    "summary": "A bolster-cover; made of ikat tabby cotton cloth.  Striped fabric: one stripe has a line of cream geometric motifs on a blue &#039;ground&#039;, framed by two narrower stripes of identical colouring with triangular motifs.  All separated by yellow silk (?) and solid brown cotton stripes.  At one side the rectangular-shaped cover is stitched onto pleated cloth made of the same fabric, finishing with large, round, padded &#039;button&#039;, made from used, more worn, ikat cloth.  The opposite side, the opening, is also pleated.  Unused?",
